Example 1 – simple division
  Calculate &frac{2}{3} ÷ &frac{1}{4}
  Keep &frac{2}{3}, change to ×, flip &frac{1}{4} to &frac{4}{1}
  &frac{2}{3} × &frac{4}{1} = &frac{8}{3}
  = 2&frac{2}{3}
  = 2&frac{2}{3}
  (Flip the second fraction then multiply across.)

Example 2 – both non-unit
  Calculate &frac{3}{5} ÷ &frac{2}{7}
  Keep &frac{3}{5}, change to ×, flip &frac{2}{7} to &frac{7}{2}
  &frac{3}{5} × &frac{7}{2} = &frac{21}{10}
  = 2&frac{1}{10}
  = 2&frac{1}{10}
  (Multiply numerators and denominators separately.)

✓ To divide by a fraction, flip the second fraction and multiply
✗ &frac{2}{3} ÷ &frac{1}{4} = &frac{2}{12}
✓ The reciprocal of &frac{3}{5} is &frac{5}{3}
✗ Dividing by a fraction always gives a smaller answer
✓ &frac{1}{2} ÷ 3 = &frac{1}{6}

